#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:15
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:24
msgid "Privacy"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:19
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:26
msgid "Effective date: 19 August 2026"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:25
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:30
msgid "About this policy"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:26
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:32
msgid ""
"This policy explains how Stricknani handles information when you use a "
"Stricknani web instance or the companion Android app."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:27
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:38
msgid ""
"Stricknani is self-hosted software. The operator of the instance you use "
"is responsible for its deployment, configuration, backups, and legal "
"obligations. This page describes the default behavior of the software and"
" is not a promise about every deployment."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:31
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:46
msgid "Who is responsible for your data?"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:32
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:48
msgid ""
"For a self-hosted installation, the person or organization operating that"
" installation is the controller of the data stored there. The Stricknani "
"project does not receive data from independent self-hosted instances."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:33
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:54
msgid ""
"If you use an instance operated by somebody else, contact that operator "
"about access, deletion, retention, or other privacy requests. Questions "
"about the Stricknani software can be reported through the"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:33
#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:80
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:59
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:224
msgid "GitHub issue tracker"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:37
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:65
msgid "Information handled by the web app"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:39
msgid ""
"Account information: your email address, a password hash, and account "
"security state such as token version."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:40
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:74
msgid ""
"Knitting content: projects, yarn entries, notes, instructions, "
"categories, steps, attachments, profile images, and other information you"
" choose to store."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:41
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:80
msgid ""
"Authentication information: a session cookie for browser login and "
"personal access tokens for API or Android access. Token values are shown "
"only when they are created; the server stores a hash for later "
"verification."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:42
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:86
msgid ""
"Operational information: application and import logs may contain "
"timestamps, routes, status information, error details, and identifiers "
"needed to operate and troubleshoot the instance. The operator chooses log"
" destinations and retention."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:47
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:95
msgid "Why this information is used"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:48
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:97
msgid ""
"The web app uses this information to authenticate you, provide project "
"and yarn management, synchronize API clients, serve your authorized "
"media, process imports, protect the service, and diagnose failures. It "
"does not sell your information or use it for advertising."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:52
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:105
msgid "Android app and offline data"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:53
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:107
msgid ""
"The Android app connects only to the Stricknani server URL that you "
"configure. It stores that URL and your personal access token locally, "
"encrypted at rest, and does not ask for or store your Stricknani account "
"password."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:54
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:113
msgid ""
"Projects, yarn entries, and their photos are cached on the device so the "
"app can work offline. Offline edits may be queued locally and are sent to"
" your configured server when synchronization resumes. Removing the app or"
" clearing its application data removes the local cache according to "
"Android behavior."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:55
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:119
msgid ""
"The Android app has no analytics, advertising, tracking, or crash-"
"reporting service of its own. Data sent during synchronization goes to "
"the server you configured."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:59
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:157
msgid "Optional external services"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:60
msgid ""
"A deployment may enable integrations that send limited information "
"outside the Stricknani instance. For example, an AI provider may receive "
"material submitted for AI-assisted pattern import, an archive service may"
" receive a URL when you request an archive snapshot, and Sentry may "
"receive diagnostic events when an operator configures it."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:61
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:165
msgid ""
"These integrations are optional and controlled by the instance operator. "
"Their providers process information under their own terms and privacy "
"policies; review those policies before enabling or using the related "
"feature."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:62
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:171
msgid ""
"The web interface itself uses locally served assets and does not require "
"an analytics or advertising network."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:66
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:179
msgid "Storage, retention, and deletion"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:67
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:181
msgid ""
"The instance stores account data and content in its configured database "
"and media storage. There is no universal retention period: the operator "
"determines retention, backups, log rotation, and whether deleted data "
"remains in backups for a time."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:68
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:187
msgid ""
"You can manage your content and revoke personal access tokens through the"
" available features. To request deletion or an export of account data, "
"contact the instance operator. Deleting content or an account does not "
"necessarily remove copies already retained in backups, logs, or external "
"services."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:72
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:195
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:73
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:197
msgid ""
"Stricknani uses password hashing, access checks, CSRF protection, upload "
"validation, and security response headers. Operators should use HTTPS, "
"protect application secrets, restrict access to the database and media "
"volume, keep the software and host updated, and configure backups "
"securely."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:74
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:203
msgid ""
"No software can guarantee absolute security. The security and "
"confidentiality of a self-hosted installation also depend on the "
"operator, hosting environment, network, integrations, and devices used to"
" access it."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:78
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:211
msgid "Your choices and contact"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:79
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:213
msgid ""
"You may choose what to enter, upload, synchronize, or send to optional "
"integrations. You may stop using the Android app, clear its local data, "
"revoke API tokens, and contact the relevant instance operator about your "
"rights under applicable law."
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:80
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:219
msgid ""
"For software questions or privacy concerns that relate to the project, "
"use the"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:84
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:230
msgid "Changes to this policy"
msgstr ""

#: stricknani/templates/legal/privacy.html:85
#: web/src/routes/privacy/+page.svelte:232
msgid ""
"This policy may be updated when Stricknani behavior or integrations "
"change. The current version is published at this URL. Check the effective"
" date above for the latest revision."
msgstr ""

